    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a74f385c-9869-5fa7-8c84-c8982d1eab48",
      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{22}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{22}=6+(-3)\\cdot (2)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C &=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
